<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2d-taiyuan-2026-11-18 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2D / Unknown Payload (Taiyuan LC-9) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. LL2 id e0a11eb1-0bda-4872-b36b-140247fd5c60, status Go, NET 2026-11-18T22:50:00Z (Wed 18 Nov 2:50 p.m. PST), window 22:43-23:05Z, payload and orbit Unknown.
Event times: SAST TYPICAL LM-2D sequence via https://sat.huijiwiki.com/wiki/长征二号丁 (same vehicle file as lm2d-jiuquan): pitch-over 17.0 s, S1 cutoff 153.9 s, sep 155.1 s, fairing 185.1 s, S2 main cutoff 324.1 s, S2 vernier cutoff 705.1 s. Typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s. Payload separation is not in this file.
Azimuth 188.65 deg: mean great-circle bearing from LL2 pad LC-9 (38.863128N 111.589567E) to NOTAM Q-line centres. A5897/26 centre 33 deg 22 min N, 110 deg 36 min E, bearing 188.57 deg, 618 km (https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-ZLHW-A5897%2F26). A5898/26 centre 30 deg 15 min N, 110 deg 04 min E, bearing 188.73 deg, 968 km (https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-ZHWH-A5898%2F26).
Orbit ASSUMED: 500 km circular SSO-class. The target orbit is not published. Circular insertion at vernier cutoff is ASSUMED. Non-rotating inclination from this azimuth is about 96.7 deg; SSO at 500 km is about 97.4 deg.
Altitude knots (t s: km; times = published typical sequence, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times rounded to 0.1 km, final = ASSUMED 500 km orbit): 0:0, 17:0.3, 153.9:43.6, 155.1:44.2, 185.1:58.6, 324.1:173.4, 705.1:500
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.667 km/s (circular v at 500 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+705.1 s. File ends at final cutoff.
Pad (LL2 Launch Complex 9): 38.863128N 111.589567E. The LL2 Taiyuan location centroid is 38.8491N 111.608E; no pad table in this repo. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=188.65 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-18T22:50:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
